jrk|n|An instrument, formerly much used for showing the time of day from the shadow of a style or gnomon on a graduated arc or surface; esp., a sundial; but there are lunar and astral dials. The style or gnomon is usually parallel to the earth's axis, but the dial plate may be either horizontal or vertical. ; The graduated face of a timepiece, on which the time of day is shown by pointers or hands. ; A miner's compass.	n:1wkt,47,1~1wkt,47,1
jrk|a|To measure with a dial. ; To survey with a dial.	j:uba,95,3;110k,89,2~uba,95,3;110k,89,2
jrl|n|Means or mode of expressing thoughts; language; tongue; form of speech. ; The form of speech of a limited region or people, as distinguished from ether forms nearly related to it; a variety or subdivision of a language; speech characterized by local peculiarities or specific circumstances; as, the Ionic and Attic were dialects of Greece; the Yorkshire dialect; the dialect of the learned.	a:16lz,70,5;ocd,52,3;k06,40,6;1wir,32,2~k06,40,6;16lz,70,5;ocd,52,3;1wir,32,2
