k0o|n|The state of being difficult, or hard to do; hardness; arduousness; -- opposed to easiness or facility; as, the difficulty of a task or enterprise; a work of difficulty. ; Something difficult; a thing hard to do or to understand; that which occasions labor or perplexity, and requires skill and perseverance to overcome, solve, or achieve; a hard enterprise; an obstacle; an impediment; as, the difficulties of a science; difficulties in theology. ; A controversy; a falling out; a disagreement; an objection; a cavil. ; Embarrassment of affairs, especially financial affairs; -- usually in the plural; as, to be in difficulties.	a:q0o,52,3;p31,48,5;7mr,47,3;1p8j,44,4;qob,43,5;rsg,37,5;vrg,34,13;210p,33,7;1tql,31,6;1kr8,29,3~1w1v,11,33;vrg,34,13;1oab,25,7;210p,33,7;1tql,31,6;17jj,25,6;rsg,37,5;zw,25,5;p31,48,5;qob,43,5	v:1hig,54,4;10te,51,4;26qt,46,1;10ti,42,3;20vb,42,4;qsy,35,3;1ru6,10,9;rst,6,5~1ru6,10,9;rst,6,5;1hig,54,4;20vb,42,4;10te,51,4;qsy,35,3;10ti,42,3;26qt,46,1	V:1omy,78,10;ef5,77,2;1pd1,73,4;e4q,61,5;1dhr,59,4;qp0,57,5;hwj,54,4;1t6p,49,6;1pff,46,3;e9d,43,2~up1,30,15;1omy,78,10;rsy,42,8;257f,40,8;1t6p,49,6;sku,28,5;1n32,40,5;qp0,57,5;297a,14,5;1lmu,15,5	n:1065,48,3;qob,43,5;qdb,3,3;g8r,3,3~qob,43,5;g8r,3,3;qdb,3,3;1065,48,3	N:15wz,28,11~15wz,28,11
